WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 7: Tell It Another Way.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.860
Welcome to Unit 7.

3
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:13.660
This unit is called "Tell It Another Way" because you will
explore one of the most powerful tools a writer can use:

4
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:14.800
point of view.

5
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:22.440
Every story is told by someone, and the person telling
the story decides what the reader sees, hears, and feels.

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:30.960
When you change the narrator, the whole story can feel
completely different, even if the events stay exactly the same.

7
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.820
Think about a football match.

8
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.380
If the winning team tells the story, they might
say, "We played brilliantly and scored three goals!"

9
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.300
If the losing team tells the same story,
they might say, "It was a difficult day.

10
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.780
We tried our best but could not find the net."

11
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.960
The match is the same, but the feelings, the
details, and the mood are completely different.

12
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.420
That is the power of...

13
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:03.600
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

14
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:11.280
By the end of this unit, you will be able to explain what
point of view means and identify the narrator in a text.

15
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:18.500
you will also compare two versions of the same event
told from different perspectives and explain what changes.

16
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:25.100
you will also describe how changing the narrator
changes the mood, detail, and feeling of a story.

17
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.320
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

18
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:36.880
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
local, urban, rural, spacious, continent, colonial.

19
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.800
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

20
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.500
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

21
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:55.440
The reading sequence includes Tell It Another Way:
source text 1 and Tell It Another Way: source text 2.

22
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.100
Read actively.

23
00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:02.020
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.160
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:11.160
The first language focus is What
Does It Mean to Express an Opinion?.

26
00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.320
An opinion is what you think or believe about something.

27
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.640
It is not a fact — it is your own view.

28
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.440
Different people can have different opinions
about the same thing, and that is perfectly fine.

29
00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:30.460
Sharing our opinions helps us have good discussions,
understand each other, and learn new ideas.

30
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.640
A fact is something that can be proved true or false.

31
00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.900
An opinion is something that someone thinks or feels.

32
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:45.080
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

33
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.260
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Hot-Seating (Character Interview).

34
00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.580
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

35
00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.460
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

36
00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.160
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

37
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.700
You are ready to begin.

38
00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:12.300
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

39
00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.940
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

40
00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:21.000
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
